{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-29T11:11:27.718Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"fa01d73dc577fc95116854e8","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-29T11:11:27.718Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"PR 189 round 4 replaces the provider-less legacy and unit-aware atomic import writers with one forward-only per-item coordinator. Production imports no longer invoke or resume content-only workspace/item transaction journals, perform compensation, or resurrect reserved identities. The old atomic flag and importLinearAtomic API name delegate to forward-only behavior; fresh SDK observations decide unchanged/conflict outcomes. Existing journals remain audit records for explicit operator inspection. This addresses the live frozen-replay path tracked here; leave this item open for orchestrator verification and any historical-journal guidance. The SDK final read-to-write window (#1576/#1620) remains documented."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-29T11:11:27.718Z"}],"before_hash":"d53edfd775b489c5a7db20193f1613da4f7db5038b4a96f68d48521d40ccb48b","after_hash":"371c0d86b61f5b2a1db788f5156eedd5e73cb65ed943291ac47e9436a184d5fc","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"b10ce30ab66653531c9597a516565b982062279792d18b81512e0110ad2ecd46"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-30T00:42:54.569Z","author":"claude-hub","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"0efcf6fa5f6489abf1ec4ce5","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.312","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-30T00:42:54.569Z","author":"claude-hub","text":"Correction to the previous comment (the earlier record stays as written): the old atomic flag and the importLinearAtomic API name do NOT delegate to forward-only behavior. assertLinearImportMode (index.ts) throws LinearAtomicRefusal (atomic_unavailable) before any work whenever atomic is requested and forwardOnly is not exactly true; importLinearAtomic calls it with atomic=true, and the linear sync/import commands apply it to --atomic. Only an explicit forwardOnly: true / --forward-only accepts per-item application. test/import-boundaries.test.ts ('atomic class: every explicit stronger-guarantee request refuses...') asserts this; README and docs/estimate-units.md say the same."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-30T00:42:54.569Z"}],"before_hash":"371c0d86b61f5b2a1db788f5156eedd5e73cb65ed943291ac47e9436a184d5fc","after_hash":"3c90418446fbed862aa2f4af925f82ee7ac2bffa9a5c4dae975f73c1d87f153d","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"ba4f19a23a15ab4046ae8f765b24d7f4ba4434ded4735e799a0c193549601f53"}
